  "mathematical_derivation": "355,865 tabular test flows - (8 capture files * 4 dropped boundary flows) = 355,833 flows. For sequence length T = 5, constructing causal sequences strictly within each capture file requires dropping the first (T - 1) = 4 flows of each file so sequences never cross unrelated files. Across the 8 CIC-IDS2017 capture files, exactly 8 * 4 = 32 boundary flows are excluded for sequence models. Every single one of the 32 dropped boundary flows was a benign baseline flow (zero attack flows dropped). Tabular detectors (Random Forest and Phase 2 offline flow replay) consume per-flow tabular features and therefore evaluate the complete, unconstrained 355,865 test population.",
